    "GeoffMillerAZ/fathom: 2 tool-oracle entries on files fathom does not read (ingest's gates, discovery's exclusions) were left out of scope (§1.4): the config of the vendored agentic-kit mirror, which fathom's own .fathomignore leaves out (O500); it is measured as the subject GeoffMillerAZ/fathom (third_party/agentic-kit), rooted there",
    "oracle tiers (wave fx item fmt, calibration/oracles/fathom-config): sym_* (L1) and ref_* (L2) are tier C. The oracle is Python 3.14.7's tomllib, a TOML decode and not fathom's go-toml/v2 or internal/config's loader: it reads what each file writes, not what the schema means, so every metric caps at good (design §1.3). Lines come from the oracle's own line scanner (range_agreement 1 over 58 entities). Structure is graded beside it, tier A and not a metric: cue vet -d '#Config' schema/config/schema.cue over each decoded file passes on all 5 files",
    "the subjects are small: 4 config files and 58 entities. Neither the repository's own config nor agentic-kit's writes a profile or a default_profile, so the 4 reference pairs (L2) are all on the two schema-valid fixtures in calibration/oracles/fathom-config/fixtures, which are in-repo files (their subject sha is the fathom commit they were measured at, not a pinned external repository), and L2 good rests on them (O501)",
